Article 24-2 (Integrated Purchasing of Fire Equipment)
(1) The head of a fire service agency may conclude a contract for jointly ordering fire equipment with other fire service agencies in any of the following cases, as determined by the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency:
1. Where the purchase and supply of fire equipment are urgent to ensure the safety of operators of fire equipment;
2. Where the leading introduction of new technologies or new products is necessary to strengthen disaster response;
3. Where purchasing is difficult because demand for the fire equipment is low or preparing specifications is difficult;
4. Other cases where the Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency deems it difficult for fire service agencies to purchase fire equipment individually.

(2) The heads of fire service agencies involved in concluding a contract under paragraph (1) shall cooperate in matters necessary for concluding the contract.

(3) The Fire Commissioner of the National Fire Agency may assist in affairs concerning conclusion of contracts under paragraph (1), if necessary to improve the efficiency of purchasing fire equipment.

[This Article Newly Inserted on June 11, 2024]
